{
  "_readme": "SOURCE OF TRUTH for the C64 game feasibility matrix. Edit this file, then run `node scripts/gen-capability-matrix.mjs` (or `yarn gen:matrix`) to regenerate docs/game-feasibility-matrix.html. Each game lists the capabilities it `needs` (ids from `capabilities`); a game with an empty `needs` is buildable Now. The Buildable verdict (Now/Soon/Blocked), the summary tallies, and the per-capability unlock counts are all DERIVED by the generator from `needs` + each capability `tier` — never stored here. Confidence keys: known|inferred|low. Diff: S|M|L|XL.",
  "meta": {
    "title": "Blend65 — C64 Game Feasibility Matrix",
    "lastUpdated": "2026-07-17",
    "refreshWith": "/update_capability"
  },
  "intro": {
    "purpose": [
      "A capability-grounded assessment of whether 100 well-known Commodore 64 games could be built **faithfully** with the Blend65 toolchain. Every game is judged by the **capabilities it needs** — compiler, an optimizer for speed, sound, input, graphics loading, math — and which of those exist today. A game is buildable **Now** when every capability it needs already ships, **Soon** when it only waits on a *planned* capability, and **Blocked** when it needs one that *isn’t planned*.",
      "**No sugarcoating.** A game is only **Now** if it can be built as the original *played* — right engine, right controls, clean in-language audio, no missing essentials, and no dropping to hand-poked machine-code bytes. A reduced-scope demake is not \"Now\"."
    ]
  },
  "capabilities": [
    {
      "id": "compiler",
      "name": "Compiler & language",
      "tier": "available",
      "blurb": "The frozen v3 language compiles end-to-end to 6502 (RD-18 complete). Every game needs it; none is blocked on it any more."
    },
    {
      "id": "optimizer",
      "name": "Optimizer (speed)",
      "tier": "planned",
      "blurb": "A cycle-budget optimizer. Unlocks smooth per-frame scrolling and sprite multiplexing (>8 sprites) within the frame budget."
    },
    {
      "id": "sound-music",
      "name": "Sound — music & SFX",
      "tier": "available",
      "blurb": "SID music and effects, written in-language and poked to the sound registers each frame."
    },
    {
      "id": "sound-sampled",
      "name": "Sound — sampled speech",
      "tier": "planned",
      "blurb": "Digitized speech / sample playback with tight timing. Doable in-language; an effort, not a language gap."
    },
    {
      "id": "joystick",
      "name": "Joystick / input",
      "tier": "available",
      "blurb": "Reading the joysticks and keyboard via the CIA ports with `peek`."
    },
    {
      "id": "graphics-loading",
      "name": "Graphics / data loading",
      "tier": "unplanned",
      "blurb": "Disk multi-load, streaming, and data sets larger than 64 KB. No loader / KERNAL story exists yet."
    },
    {
      "id": "math",
      "name": "Math (fixed-point / float)",
      "tier": "planned",
      "blurb": "Fractional math. No floating point in the language; a fixed-point library would make hand-rolled physics clean."
    },
    {
      "id": "asm",
      "name": "Hand-tuned asm",
      "tier": "unplanned",
      "blurb": "Linking cycle-exact hand-written assembly for 50 fps showcases and real-time 3D. Deferred, unscheduled."
    },
    {
      "id": "indirect-calls",
      "name": "Indirect calls / dispatch",
      "tier": "unplanned",
      "blurb": "Function pointers, jump tables, VM-style dispatch (SCUMM engines, calling a ripped `.sid` player). Deferred, unscheduled."
    }
  ],
