  "howToRead": [
    "**Buildable?** rolls up the capabilities a game needs: **✅ Now** — all of them ship today · **🟡 Soon** — the only ones missing are *planned* · **❌ Blocked** — it needs a capability that *isn’t planned*.",
    "**Needs** lists the missing capabilities, most-blocking first. A **Now** game needs nothing it doesn’t already have (shown as `—`).",
    "**The capability status board** above is the lever: ship one capability and *every* game waiting on it moves. The unlock counts show how many.",
    "**Difficulty** (S/M/L/XL) is implementation effort, independent of buildability. **Confidence** — ✅ internals known · ⚠️ inferred from archetype · 🔴 low.",
    "**Faithfulness bar is strict**: \"Now\" means the original *as played* — not a reduced-scope demake that drops the smooth scroll, the disk content, or the exact soundtrack."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "**Original-soundtrack footnote.** In-language SID music and effects are clean (*Sound — music & SFX*, available now). Reproducing a *ripped* `.sid` tune byte-for-byte means calling its own machine-code player routine, which needs **Indirect calls** — so a byte-faithful ripped soundtrack carries an implicit indirect-calls dependency. It is not added to every row."
  ],
  "summaryNote": "The **Blocked** titles all need a capability that isn’t planned — **graphics loading** (the disk RPGs, SCUMM adventures, Cinemaware, Epyx multi-event sports, the streamed Last Ninjas), **hand-tuned asm** (real-time 3D and the 50 fps showcases: Elite, Out Run, Mayhem in Monsterland), or **indirect calls** (SCUMM dispatch). No optimizer reaches them — they need a new capability, not faster code. See the unlock table at the bottom.",
