  "inversion": {
    "intro": "What shipping each capability unlocks — the number of the 100 titles that list it in their **Needs**. Read this to decide what to build next.",
    "rows": [
      {
        "id": "optimizer",
        "impact": "**The single biggest unlock.** Moves nearly every perf-bound scroller, shmup and brawler from Blocked/Soon toward Now. Already planned."
      },
      {
        "id": "graphics-loading",
        "impact": "**The biggest hard-gap unlock.** Frees the entire disk catalogue — the RPGs (Ultima, Bard’s Tale, Pool of Radiance), SCUMM adventures, Cinemaware, Epyx multi-event sports, and the streamed Last Ninjas. No story exists today."
      },
      {
        "id": "asm",
        "impact": "The 50 fps / vector ceiling the optimizer alone can’t reach: real-time 3D (Elite, Mercenary), sprite-scaling racers (Out Run), the full-colour scroll showcase (Mayhem in Monsterland)."
      },
      {
        "id": "math",
        "impact": "Fractional physics: golf (Leaderboard), marble/ball physics (Marble Madness, Spindizzy), pseudo-3D road math. Hand-rollable today (why several are Soon, not Blocked); a library makes them clean."
      },
      {
        "id": "sound-sampled",
        "impact": "Digitized speech (Impossible Mission-class). Doable in-language with tight timing; an effort, not a language gap."
      },
      {
        "id": "indirect-calls",
        "impact": "True VM / dispatch-table engines (SCUMM). Also the clean way to call a ripped `.sid` player and any jump-table dispatch — a broad quality-of-life unlock beyond the raw count."
      }
    ],
    "bottomLine": "**Sequencing:** the **optimizer** first (planned; unlocks the most and the flashiest arcade action), then a **graphics-loading / disk** story (frees the entire \"epic\" catalogue the optimizer can never touch), then **hand-tuned asm** + a **fixed-point math** library for the 3D / showcase tier."
  },
  "provenance": [
    "**The list is curated, not a sourced ranking.** These are 100 well-known, category-spanning C64 titles — not \"the top 100\" by any measured metric (sales, Zzap!64 score, Lemon64 votes). Swap freely with `/update_capability`.",
    "**Verdicts anchor on *engine archetype*, the real feasibility driver**, then adjust for a title’s specifics. Where a title’s internals are inferred rather than known, the **Conf** column says so (⚠️/🔴) — treat those rows as archetype estimates, not reverse-engineered fact.",
    "**Faithfulness bar is strict**: \"Now\" means the original *as played*. A reduced-scope demake that captures the feel but drops the smooth scroll, the multiplexed sprite count, the disk-streamed content, or the exact soundtrack is not \"Now\" — even when it would be a perfectly good game.",
    "**Memory pressure is folded into difficulty, not a capability.** A title that strains 64 KB but fits with effort is not \"blocked\"; one whose data genuinely exceeds RAM needs *graphics loading* (disk), and is marked so."
  ],
  "footer": "Maintained via `/update_capability`. When a capability ships (the optimizer lands, a disk / loader story arrives, fixed-point math or asm-linking ships), re-run it to move every game waiting on that capability and refresh the counts."
}
